<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Raj Singh I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1629">1629</a>–<a href="/years/1680">1680</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-raj">Raj</a> Singh I was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maharana">Maharana</a> of Mewar from 1652 to 1680. He opposed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangzeb">Aurangzeb</a>'s reimposition of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jizya">jizya</a> in 1679 and supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rathore">Rathores of Marwar</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajputs">Rajput</a> war against the Mughal emperor. He gave shelter to the image of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shrinathji">Shrinathji</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nathdwara">Nathdwara</a> in 1672 and built the great reservoir of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajsamand-lake">Rajsamand Lake</a>, whose embankment carries the Raj Prashasti, one of the longest <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> inscriptions in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/raj-singh-i.jpg" alt="Raj Singh I" width="320" height="476" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Raja Ravi Varma · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raja_Ravi_Varma,_Maharana_Raj_Singh_-_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
